# .env.example — template for environment variables.
# (An "environment variable" is a named setting the app reads at startup,
# used for secrets and per-environment configuration so they never live in code.)
#
# Copy this file to `.env` and fill in real values. `.env` is git-ignored;
# real secrets must NEVER be committed to the repository.
#
# Stage 0 has no running application, so nothing here is used yet.
# Entries are added as later stages introduce them, always with a comment
# explaining what the value is and where to get it.

# --- placeholder (no values required in Stage 0) ---
